1. Who made it. ASTRA is a work of JoseGR (https://github.com/jgr-ry).
   The program, its design, its name and its logo belong to JoseGR.

2. What you may do. Install and use ASTRA, free of charge, on your own
   computers for personal use.

3. What you may not do without JoseGR's written permission:
   - copy or hand out ASTRA or its installer (if someone wants it, give
     them the official link: https://github.com/jgr-ry/ASTRA-UPDATES);
   - sell, rent, lend for money or sublicense it;
   - modify, decompile or disassemble it, except where the law allows it
     even though this licence forbids it;
   - remove or change its authorship or licence notices.

4. It is a beta. ASTRA is being tested and may fail. It is provided
   "as is", without warranty of any kind. To the extent the law allows,
   JoseGR is not liable for any damage or data loss arising from its use.

5. Your data. ASTRA has no server and no accounts and collects no data
   for JoseGR. What it keeps stays on your computer. What it sends to
   other services (the AI you choose, your integrations, the weather,
   your calendars, updates) only leaves when you use those features, with
   your keys and under those services' terms. All the details are in
   Settings › Privacy & security.

6. Third-party components. ASTRA includes open-source components that
   keep their own licences (Settings › About › Open-source components).
   This licence does not limit the rights those licences give you over
   those components.

7. Updates. ASTRA can look for new versions (switch it off in
   Settings › Updates). Each version is covered by this licence or by
   the one that comes with it.

8. Termination. If you break this licence it ends, and you must uninstall
   ASTRA.
